# Model separation

There is no Request / DTO / Response / AutoMapper stack. Do not add one.

| Kind | Where | Role |
|------|--------|------|
| Domain type | `src/Pilldue.Business/Domain` | The model. EF maps these types directly |
| Port | `src/Pilldue.Business/Ports` | What hosts and services need from storage |
| EF mapping | `src/Pilldue.Data/PilldueDbContext.cs` | Table names, keys, columns |
| Persistence | `src/Pilldue.Data/Ef*.cs` | Port implementations |
| In-memory fake | `src/Pilldue.Business/Memory` | Tests and early composition |
| Screen | `src/Pilldue.UI.Wpf` | Input and display. No stock or calendar math |
| UI catalogs | `src/Pilldue.Business/Localization` | English and Serbian strings for the WPF screens |

A new persisted field is a property on the Business type, then EF configuration and a migration in Data, then the port method if a use case needs it. UI reaches it through `IPilldueApp` or an existing Business service.

Config (UI language) is a JSON file via `IAppConfigStore`, not an EF table.
